## Abstract

This report presents the development and implementation of a machine learning-based fake news detection system that classifies news articles as authentic or fabricated. The system employs Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques combined with Logistic Regression to achieve an accuracy of 98.79% and F1-score of 98.75%. Built using Streamlit for web deployment, the application provides real-time classification with confidence scoring and feature importance analysis. The project addresses the growing concern of misinformation in digital media by providing an accessible tool for preliminary news authenticity assessment.

**Keywords:** Fake News Detection, Machine Learning, Natural Language Processing, TF-IDF, Logistic Regression, Text Classification

